Or a new kind of shop: The barber/ hairdresser. You can pay the barber
an unreasonable amount of zorkmids for either a shave & haircut or
styling & blowdry (depending on player gender) and get a +1 Cha boost
in return. Obviously the game shouldn't let you stack these, so the
CHA boost disappears after a few thousand turns or when your hair gets
messed up by a major combat/burning/freezing/falling rock
trap/rust-trap hitting your head/swim/polymorph/explosion. Once the
cha boost is gone you'd be eligible for another tidy-up.

You'd be ineligible for a a haircut if you are polymorphed into
something without a head, although it would be a pain working out
which creatures had a head but no hair (D,B,:,;,c etc). Barbers would
get upset if you enter the shop in the form of a d,f or u. ("There's a
pet grooming salon on Dlevel 15, now get out of my shop") and perhaps
charge extra if you are polymorphed into something unreasonably hairy
(yeti).

Obviously you'd have to remove your headgear for a haircut, so maybe
barbers could also have a talent for removing cursed helmets. (So that
they are actually useful for something in nethack) However, if you
were wearing a cursed helmet, then there's a chance that all the hair
that gets cut off will turn into a hair golem.

Every once in a while (1/100 chance) the barber would make a mistake
and mess up your hair completely, resulting in a -1 Cha modifier and
you (probably) getting your money back. Also, he might occasionally
nick you with the scissors/ razor for 1 point of HP. Finally, during
your session the barber would dispense minor fortunes (mostly false)
interspersed with "are you going on holiday this year?" and random
gossip about who in the dungeon is sleeping with who and so on.

Unlike regular shopkeepers there wouldn't be much reason for barbers
to carry huge amounts of money, but working in a dungeon you'd expect
them to carry a wand or something for self defence, or at least be
very dangerous #twoweaponing their scissors & razor (new items).

You might also have the occasional "demon barber" who appears at first
to be a real barber, but once you're in the chair he turns into a &
and surprise attacks you with his scissors & razor, getting a surprise
first hit. There should be subtle ways of identifying these in
advance, including a ring or protection from shapechangers.

